# Cloudflare Pages response headers
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# HTML, CSS and our own JS use Cloudflare Pages' default caching
# (max-age=0, must-revalidate, with ETags), so changes show up straight
# away and unchanged files cost only a quick 304. Only the vendored
# three.js, whose contents never change at a given path, is cached
# long-term. If three.js is upgraded, put it in a new folder.
#
# Don't set Cache-Control in /* as well: Pages joins duplicate headers
# from overlapping rules with a comma.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: interest-cohort=()

/assets/js/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
